   "description": "The cgroup files on pve01, live. CPU weight: the share of CPU under contention (100 is the default; double it, double the share). CPUs: a container's cores are a cpuset, the CPUs its processes may run on; a VM's are virtual CPUs, so it has none. Memory limit: above it the kernel kills a process (OOM) inside the guest; memory high: above it the kernel reclaims cache and slows the guest down first. A VM's memory is fixed by QEMU instead, so its cgroup has no memory limit. none: no limit set.",
